mushaf page fonts (QPC v2, and the QPC V4 Tajweed colour fonts via the Quranic
Universal Library), the tajweed rule data (quran.com API), the Amiri fonts and the MihrabMedallion font derived from
Amiri Quran (SIL OFL 1.1), and the recitation audio are
the property of their respective authors and are used under their own terms.
The Latin-letter transliterations shown under an ayah are from risan/quran-json
(https://github.com/risan/quran-json, CC BY-SA 4.0; generated from the Arabic,
and corrected by this app in fourteen ayahs listed in
src/quran/transliterationCorrections.ts) and, in Turkish, by Muhammet Abay
(from Tanzil's list of translations, https://tanzil.net/trans/, under Tanzil's
terms). They are downloaded on request and are not part of the app's source.
The hadith are downloaded on request and are not part of the app: texts,
translations, explanations and lessons from HadeethEnc.com (the Encyclopedia of
Translated Prophetic Hadiths, https://hadeethenc.com), republished unmodified
with credit; an-Nawawi's Forty in Arabic from fawazahmed0/hadith-api
(https://github.com/fawazahmed0/hadith-api); and the nine books in Arabic from
Open-Hadith-Data (https://github.com/mhashim6/Open-Hadith-Data), made available
under the Open Database License 1.0 (https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/),
its contents under the Database Contents License 1.0. Mihrab's copies, published
as assets of the data-hadith-v1 release of this repository, are derived from
those sources by scripts/hadith/build-packs.js and are offered under the same
terms.
The Garmin watch face's fonts (garmin/watchface/resources/fonts) are bitmaps
made from Tektur, copyright 2023 The Tektur Project Authors, under the SIL Open
Font License 1.1 (garmin/tools/fonts/OFL.txt).

THIRD-PARTY CODE KEPT IN THIS TREE
----------------------------------
The notification engine is Notifee 9.1.8, copyright 2016-present Invertase
Limited, under the Apache License 2.0: its Android core and React Native
bridge in android/alerts/, its iOS ones in ios/Alerts/, its JavaScript in
src/native/notifee/, each with the licence beside it. It is no longer
maintained upstream and is kept here so it can be. Changed from the release,
so far: the two Android manifests are one; the build files are this
project's; NotificationAndroidStyleModel.java names the overload it calls
(bigLargeIcon((Bitmap) null)); in the TypeScript, one type React Native no
longer exports is declared locally, four values are asserted non-null, lint
comments that no longer apply are gone, the unused web stub
(NotifeeNativeModule.web.ts) is removed, and documentation links in comments
are written without their scheme (this project's network test reads every
host named in src/ as one the app may contact). Files changed later say so in the
file.

